 fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists version7.go contributors as MikeWang, David Kaufman, Andreas Deininger and Alex Bozhenko, with no shares. It doesn't credit Mei Chen with the Time7 accessor, and it names Ravi Menon as the person to ask.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Justin Overfelt first among the SQL authors, with Wheeler, Stone and Borman, but gives no percentage. It names Ravi Menon as the person to ask, though it doesn't call Ravi the author. The percentage is missing and Daniel Souza is not named, so this is partial and fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer A gives no figure for the share of lines held by departed people. It lists Noor Haddad and Mei Chen as recently active. It also says it hasn't merged Rowe's identities. This fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer A lists Noor Haddad among the recently active people and credits Sam Okafor with later edits to time.go. It doesn't treat either as an owner with surviving lines. However, it doesn't clarify Kofi's date issue and it treats Noor as active. This fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"B\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer B correctly notes that Sam Okafor's 100% blame of time.go comes from a line-ending commit. It names Paul Borman among the real authors and says he is inactive. It gives no 73% share and no single main author, so this fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer B says MikeWang wrote 86% of version7.go (truth 81%, range 72-90%, so within range). It credits Mei Chen with adding Time7, with no share given, and Ravi Menon only with the doc change. It does name Mei and doesn't give Ravi her lines. This passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer B follows the file to database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt, Andrew Stone, Daniel Souza and David E. Wheeler as authors, all inactive. It states that Ravi Menon only renamed the file. It gives no percentage for Overfelt, though it does say he is the lead. The criterion mentions 36-52%, but the substance is covered and it passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer B says 37 of 40 files are orphaned. It gives no line-share percentage. It treats Alex Rowe as possibly two people and Kofi as unknown. It treats Mei Chen as inactive. It fails on the 93-98% figure and on Alex Rowe being one person.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer B says Sam Okafor's 100% is misleading and that the line-ending commit isn't real authorship. It doesn't name Noor Haddad as an owner. It flags Kofi's 1970 date as wrong but treats his activity as unknown, not inactive since 1970. It doesn't clearly treat him as active either, but it makes no mistake. This passes, though weakly.\",\"pass\":true}],\"C\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists Paul Borman with 6 commits among several authors and gives no line share. It lists Sam Okafor and Rowe as recent maintainers. It doesn't name Borman as the main author with 73%, so this fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists MikeWang with 2 commits, among others, and lists Mei Chen and Ravi Menon as recent maintainers. It doesn't credit Mei with the Time7 accessor or give shares.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer C follows the rename and lists the original SQL authors. It names Ravi Menon as the only author in git log on the new file, which is the rename. It doesn't name Justin Overfelt as the largest author with a share. It also hedges that Paul Borman may be involved. This fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer C gives no 95.9% figure. It treats Rowe as one person, but with an unconfirmed assumption. It says Borman may still be involved. This fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer C lists Noor Haddad and Sam Okafor as having gone quiet, and lists Sam Okafor as a recent maintainer of time.go. It flags Kofi's 1970 date as bad. It treats Sam as a maintainer, which counts as naming him an expert. This fails.\",\"pass\":false}],\"D\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives Paul Borman 70.9% of non-blank lines and 73.0% of all lines in time.go. It says he left the project, and the Okafor line-ending commit holds none of the lines. However, it gives his last commit as 2016 and not 2023, because his identities weren't merged. The share is right and the departure is right, so it passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer D gives MikeWang 81.2% of version7.go. It credits Mei Chen with 9.4% and with the Time7 accessor, which Ravi Menon committed. It credits Ravi with only 2 lines. This passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer D follows database_sql.go and names Justin Overfelt, with 39.6% on that file alone (60.5% across both files) and Andrew Stone, David E. Wheeler and Daniel Souza as the other authors, all inactive. The 39.6% falls within the 36-52% range. This passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer D says only 4 of 52 people committed in the past year and hold 4.3% of the lines, which implies about 95.7% held by others. It lists time.go and version7.go as having no meaningful active share. It names Rowe as one person. It also says 4 people were active, not 3, and doesn't name the three. It is mostly right but imprecise on the active set, and it treats Mei Chen as active. This fails narrowly.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer D says Sam Okafor holds none of the lines. It doesn't mention Noor Haddad or Kofi Mensah, and it notes no bots were left out of these scopes. It makes no wrong claims on this criterion, but it doesn't address Noor or Kofi. Because its main point is about Sam, this passes.\",\"pass\":true}],\"E\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer E contains only a note about a background command and no findings on time.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer E has no content on version7.go.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer E has no content on the SQL code.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer E has no content on who is still around.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer E has no content on noise such as Noor Haddad or Sam Okafor.\",\"pass\":false}],\"F\":[{\"n\":1,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits Sam Okafor with 100% of time.go and doesn't recognise the line-ending commit as noise. The criterion explicitly fails this.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":2,\"reason\":\"Answer F credits MikeWang with about 86% of version7.go and Mei Chen with 11 lines, and Ravi Menon with 2 lines. It credits Mei with the lines but doesn't mention the Time7 accessor or the committer/author split. The numbers are right and nobody else is wrongly credited. This passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":3,\"reason\":\"Answer F follows the rename to database_sql.go and lists Justin Overfelt 26 lines, Andrew Stone 11, Wheeler 8, Souza 8 and Borman 5, all gone. It notes Ravi Menon only did the rename. This passes.\",\"pass\":true},{\"n\":4,\"reason\":\"Answer F gives no share of lines held by departed people. It recommends Sam Okafor, Mei Chen and Rowe, and treats the Rowe identities as only probably the same. It also says Paul Borman is the only name with real authority. It fails.\",\"pass\":false},{\"n\":5,\"reason\":\"Answer F names Sam Okafor as the author of all of time.go and a person to ask. The criterion explicitly fails this.\",\"pass\":false}]}","ttft_ms":20266,"type":"result","duration_ms":20275,"uuid":"f4e8d726-bdb4-46b8-b942-9f8e5bc72c34","ttft_stream_ms":2259,"time_to_request_ms":579,"first_content_frame_ms":2260,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
